---
// The three groups of Telegram signal, for the "Reading the Telegram signals"
// stage. One card per group, stacked: the label chips that belong to it (in
// the same chart colours as the Stage 1 glossary, so recognition carries
// over) sit beside the group title, then what the message means, what to do
// when it lands, and real Telegram screenshots of that message type. In the
// buy/sell group each screenshot pairs with its own explanation (shot left,
// text right) so the TP levels can be read against the message. The grouping
// principle is what the message asks of you: a look (hits), a trade (buy/sell
// signals), or caution (trend alerts). Static, so nothing to gate on
// prefers-reduced-motion.
import GuideShot from './GuideShot.astro';

// Chip colours mirror GuideLabels.astro — keep the two in sync.
const C = {
  resistance: '#9c1f5e',
  resistanceDark: '#6d1b4f',
  support: '#12997a',
  buy: '#2f6df0',
  sell: '#ee4452',
  uta: '#1397b0',
  dta: '#8b3fb0',
};
---
<div class="gsg">

  <section class="gsg-card">
    <div class="gsg-head">
      <span class="gsg-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <h3 class="gsg-title">Line hits</h3>
      <span class="gsg-chips">
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.resistance}`}>R</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.resistanceDark}`}>ER</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.resistanceDark}`}>ER2</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.support}`}>S</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.support}`}>ES</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.support}`}>ES2</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="gsg-rows">
      <div class="gsg-row">
        <p class="gsg-row-label">What it means</p>
        <p class="gsg-row-value">Price has just touched one of the channel's lines. The message names the line, the trend direction and the price — whether it's the main line or an extended one, the nature is the same.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gsg-row">
        <p class="gsg-row-label">What to do</p>
        <p class="gsg-row-value">Open the chart and watch. A hit is a heads-up that price has reached a level worth trading off, not an instruction to trade.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="gsg-shots gsg-shots-equal">
      <GuideShot narrow src="/learn/signals/resistance-hit-signal.png" caption="A resistance hit: the line, the trend direction and the price." alt="A Telegram message from the RHO Navigator Bot reading NAS100 (15m) RESISTANCE HIT, with the trend direction and price" />
      <GuideShot narrow src="/learn/signals/support-hit-signal.png" caption="And the support-side mirror." alt="A Telegram message from the RHO Navigator Bot reading NAS100 (15m) SUPPORT HIT, with the trend direction and price" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="gsg-card">
    <div class="gsg-head">
      <span class="gsg-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <h3 class="gsg-title">Buy &amp; sell signals</h3>
      <span class="gsg-chips">
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.buy}`}>B</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.buy}`}>EB</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.buy}`}>DTB</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.sell}`}>S</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.sell}`}>ES</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.sell}`}>UTB</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="gsg-rows">
      <div class="gsg-row">
        <p class="gsg-row-label">What it means</p>
        <p class="gsg-row-value">An entry cue. A buy-zone or sell-zone message spells out the whole trade — the entry price, both take-profit levels (TP1 and TP2) and the stop loss (SL). The breakout signals (DTB and UTB) flag a channel break that can start a new trend.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gsg-row">
        <p class="gsg-row-label">What to do</p>
        <p class="gsg-row-value">Check the channel before you enter: where price sits, and whether the trade goes with the trend or against it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gsg-pair">
      <GuideShot narrow src="/learn/signals/channel-buy-signal.png" caption="" alt="A Telegram buy-zone signal from the RHO Navigator Bot showing the entry price, TP1, TP2 and SL levels" />
      <div class="gsg-pair-text">
        <p class="gsg-pair-title">Channel buy signal</p>
        <p class="gsg-pair-lead">Fires at the buy zone, off the channel's support line. The targets are the next lines up:</p>
        <ul class="gsg-tps">
          <li><strong>TP1</strong> — the middle line</li>
          <li><strong>TP2</strong> — the resistance line</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gsg-pair">
      <GuideShot narrow src="/learn/signals/extended-buy-signal.png" caption="" alt="A Telegram extended buy-zone signal from the RHO Navigator Bot showing the entry price, TP1, TP2 and SL levels" />
      <div class="gsg-pair-text">
        <p class="gsg-pair-title">Extended channel buy signal</p>
        <p class="gsg-pair-lead">Fires at the extended buy zone, off the extended support below the channel — so the targets sit one line lower:</p>
        <ul class="gsg-tps">
          <li><strong>TP1</strong> — the support line</li>
          <li><strong>TP2</strong> — the middle line</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="gsg-foot">The sell signals mirror both of these on the way down. And they're the automatic version of what you'd work out by hand in the <a href="/guides/master/core-skills">core skills</a> — that's exactly why those skills matter: read the channel yourself and you can often get in earlier, at a better price, than the signal does.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="gsg-card">
    <div class="gsg-head">
      <span class="gsg-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
      <h3 class="gsg-title">Trend alerts</h3>
      <span class="gsg-chips">
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.uta}`}>UTA</span>
        <span class="gsg-chip" style={`background:${C.dta}`}>DTA</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="gsg-rows">
      <div class="gsg-row">
        <p class="gsg-row-label">What it means</p>
        <p class="gsg-row-value">The trend has just picked up speed — price is accelerating upwards (UTA) or downwards (DTA).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gsg-row">
        <p class="gsg-row-label">What to do</p>
        <p class="gsg-row-value">Nothing to enter — it's context, not a setup. Treat it as a caution: while the move is running, this isn't the moment to take a trade against it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="gsg-shots">
      <GuideShot narrow src="/learn/signals/downtrend-accelerates-signal.png" caption="A downtrend-accelerates alert: no levels, no targets — just the warning." alt="A Telegram message from the RHO Navigator Bot reading NAS100 (15m) DOWNTREND ACCELERATES, with the trend direction and price" />
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

<style>
  .gsg {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-5) 0;
  }
  .gsg-card {
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
  }

  .gsg-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .gsg-num {
    flex: none;
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--grad-primary);
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .gsg-title { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.18rem; margin: 0; }

  /* Chips sit beside the title, with breathing room; they wrap under it on
     narrow screens. */
  .gsg-chips {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 7px;
    margin-left: var(--space-2);
  }
  .gsg-chip {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 3px 12px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .gsg-rows {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .gsg-row {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--cyan);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--space-3);
  }
  .gsg-row-label {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .gsg-row-value { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.98rem; margin: 3px 0 0; }

  .gsg-shots {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
  .gsg-shots :global(.gshot) { margin: var(--space-3) 0 0; }
  .gsg-shots :global(.gshot figcaption) { text-align: center; }
  /* Equal-height shots: same height for every image in the row, so the
     captions below start on the same line. */
  .gsg-shots-equal :global(.gshot img) { height: 130px; width: auto; max-width: none; }

  /* Screenshot left, explanation right — used in the buy/sell group so each
     message's TP levels read beside the real thing. */
  .gsg-pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 340px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .gsg-pair :global(.gshot) { margin: 0; }
  .gsg-pair :global(.gshot img) { width: 100%; max-width: 340px; height: auto; }
  .gsg-pair-title { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0; }
  .gsg-pair-lead { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96rem; margin: 4px 0 0; }
  .gsg-tps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 5px;
  }
  .gsg-tps li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 22px;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .gsg-tps li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .gsg-tps strong { color: var(--ink); }

  .gsg-foot { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96rem; margin: var(--space-4) 0 0; }
  .gsg-foot a { color: var(--cyan-light); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .gsg-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .gsg-pair :global(.gshot img) { margin-inline: auto; }
    .gsg-shots { gap: var(--space-3); }
    .gsg-shots-equal :global(.gshot img) { height: auto; max-width: 100%; }
  }
</style>
